"""Industry Knowledge Packs (Startup Domain Intelligence Sprint, Phase 2; expanded in the Master
Startup Knowledge Base Sprint, Phases 2-3).

Reference data, not a reasoning engine — the same role app.agents.venture_vocabulary's `_VOCAB`
and app.agents.go_to_market_intelligence's `_GTM_VOCAB`/app.agents.feature_intelligence's
`_FEATURE_IDEAS` already play: a hand-curated, versioned, category-keyed dict of general
startup-domain knowledge, keyed by the same taxonomy app.agents.venture_vocabulary.resolve_category
already resolves every venture into (no new classifier, no new taxonomy — this sprint only added
more categories to that one existing resolver). Every fact here is qualitative, general
startup-operating knowledge — never a specific statistic, percentage, named real company, or price,
which is exactly what would turn "domain knowledge" into a fabricated claim. Deliberately excludes a
"common competitors" field: naming real companies at the category level (rather than the per-venture,
retrieval/description-derived competitors already surfaced elsewhere in the pipeline) would itself be
a fabrication risk this sprint's own rules forbid. Consumed by app.agents.startup_benchmark,
app.agents.founder_intelligence, app.agents.pricing_intelligence, and
app.agents.go_to_market_intelligence as shared reference context, never as a second, independent
recommendation engine — the actual founder-facing recommendation always still comes from those
existing modules' own venture-specific reasoning.
"""

